/* ============================================================
   contentData.js
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   Extracted from App.js (previously inlined ~29,700 lines directly in
   the main component file). All lesson/topic content (T_* constants)
   and the CONTENT registry that maps "<courseId>:<topicIndex>" to each
   topic object now live here, as a plain data module with no React or
   app logic mixed in.

   Why this move: this data made up the vast majority of App.js's
   size and was fully parsed/evaluated on every single app load
   regardless of whether a student ever opened most of these topics.
   Isolating it here does not by itself shrink what is downloaded (it
   is still imported eagerly below, so behavior is unchanged), but it
   is the necessary first step toward a real per-course lazy-load:
   once content lives in its own module boundary, a follow-up change
   can convert the CONTENT export (and the ~19 call sites in App.js
   that read it) to fetch course chunks on demand instead of all at
   once, with each screen that reads CONTENT tested afterward.
   ============================================================ */

