      q: "The neoplasia has the prevention and the screening. What are they, and why are they important?",
      body: `The neoplasia has the prevention and the screening, and the two are the important for the reduction of the burden of the cancer. The prevention includes the measures that reduce the exposure to the carcinogens, and the screening includes the tests that detect the cancer in the early stage, when it is the most treatable. The understanding of the prevention and the screening is essential for the public health and the clinical practice.

My Socratic question: the prevention includes the measures that reduce the exposure to the carcinogens, so what are the main measures, and what do they prevent?

The answer is that the prevention includes the several measures, and each prevents the specific cancers. The avoidance of the tobacco prevents the lung cancer, the the head and the neck cancer, the the bladder cancer and the the other cancers, and the smoking cessation is the single most important measure. The avoidance of the excessive alcohol prevents the liver cancer, the the oesophageal cancer and the the other cancers. The protection from the ultraviolet radiation prevents the skin cancer, and the use of the sunscreen and the avoidance of the tanning beds are the important measures. The vaccination against the human papillomavirus prevents the cervical cancer, and the vaccination against the hepatitis B virus prevents the liver cancer. And the maintenance of the healthy diet and the weight prevents the colorectal cancer, the the breast cancer and the the other cancers. The prevention is therefore the effective approach, and the understanding of the measures is essential for the public health.

The screening has its own methods and its own recommendations. The screening is the test that is performed on the asymptomatic people to detect the cancer in the early stage, and the examples include the the mammography for the breast cancer, the the colonoscopy and the the faecal occult blood test for the colorectal cancer, the the cervical smear for the cervical cancer, the the low-dose computed tomography for the lung cancer in the high-risk individuals, and the the prostate-specific antigen for the prostate cancer. The screening is important because the early detection allows the early treatment, which improves the prognosis. The screening is therefore the important part of the cancer control, and the understanding of it is essential for the clinical practice.

Crucial insight: the neoplasia has the prevention and the screening, and the two are important for the reduction of the burden of the cancer. The prevention includes the avoidance of the tobacco, the alcohol and the ultraviolet radiation, the vaccination against the human papillomavirus and the hepatitis B virus, and the healthy diet, and each prevents the specific cancers. The screening includes the mammography, the colonoscopy, the cervical smear and the other tests, and it detects the cancer in the early stage, when it is the most treatable. The prevention and the screening are the important part of the cancer control, and the understanding of them is essential for the public health.`
