    { q: "Explain the clinical importance of the digestive system.", a: "The digestive system is clinically important because it provides the nutrients that the body needs, and the diseases of the digestive system cause the significant morbidity and mortality. The understanding of the digestive physiology is essential for the diagnosis and the treatment of the diseases, including the gastritis, the peptic ulcer disease, the the malabsorption, the the inflammatory bowel disease and the the other conditions. The knowledge of the motility is the basis for the understanding of the disorders such as the the gastro-oesophageal reflux. The knowledge of the secretion is the basis for the understanding of the action of the drugs such as the proton pump inhibitors. And the knowledge of the absorption is the basis for the understanding of the nutritional deficiencies. The digestive system is therefore the central topic of the physiology." }
